            "body": "Update from a dispatched MI325 validation run (`jit-kernel-unit-test-amd` against this PR's head):\n\n- `test_store_cache.py` (pre-existing AMD registration): ✅ 57 passed\n- `test_per_token_group_quant_8bit.py` (this PR): ❌ — collects **1872 parametrized cases** and triggers a full `sgl-kernel` HIP rebuild; the 1-GPU jit-kernel job (10-min budget) fails here.\n- `test_activation.py` (this PR): not cleanly validated (job already failing).\n\nSo these JIT tests don't cleanly fit the per-commit AMD jit-kernel budget as registered. Converting this to **draft** while we reconsider scope (e.g. nightly tier, or sharding the per-token-group-quant test).\n\nSeparately, #27722 takes the lower-risk route — it migrates the AMD 2-GPU kernel tests that already run today into the registered system (1:1, zero new execution). That's the cleaner first step.",
